@prefix : <http://example.org/orexis/world/hanoi#> .
@prefix orexis: <http://example.org/orexis#> .
@prefix journal: <http://example.org/orexis/journal#> .
@prefix planning: <http://example.org/orexis/planning#> .

<> a orexis:SelfGraph .    # this document is one graph, and this is what it is

#  WHO THIS AGENT IS: the agent planning the tower, and this document is its own by the self it
#  states. Booted as "hanoi", the agent checks that this is so.
#
#  WHAT IT RUNS: it plans the tower, in planning's word, since no domain has one for what it is, and
#  nothing else. The plan is its output: it is no executor, so nothing walks the plan and the agent
#  ends `planned` once it is published (#928); and its world ships no rules, so it is no deliberator.

:hanoi a orexis:Self ;
    orexis:plays [ a planning:Planner ] .

#  IT KEEPS A JOURNAL of what happened to it, so it is a recorder (knowledge/domain/journal/recorder.md): the
#  history view and its own account of itself read what it kept. Without the role its packages say what happens
#  and nobody writes it down.
:hanoi orexis:plays [ a journal:Recorder ] .
